{%- comment -%}
  The bottle and the plant, in one frame.

  Single essences carry three images: the bottle, an Instagram graphic with text
  baked into it, and a photograph of the plant. Only the first was ever shown.
  This shows the bottle and the plant, cycling, and leaves the graphic in the
  gallery untouched.

  The plant is found by filename, not by position — it is the file called
  "pacific-essences-…", which holds on all 144 single essences. Position would
  not: on Fluorite, Iolite, Moonstone and Rutile the graphic is third and the
  plant is second.

  Expects: botanical (a media object), section_id, and optionally latin.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign lead = product.featured_media
  assign gap = section.settings.gallery_interval | default: 7 | times: 1000
  assign name_parts = product.title | split: '|'
  assign plant_name = name_parts[0] | strip
  # The alt text runs "Pacific Essences - Blue Camas - camassia quamash - …".
  # The third part is the botanical name on the flower, sea and tree essences,
  # but on the gem essences it is the category instead — minerals have no
  # binomial — so anything containing "Essence" is dropped.
  assign latin = ''
  if botanical.alt != blank
    assign alt_parts = botanical.alt | split: ' - '
    if alt_parts.size > 2
      assign latin_try = alt_parts[2] | strip
      unless latin_try contains 'Essence'
        assign latin = latin_try
      endunless
    endif
  endif
-%}

<div
  class="eg-gallery"
  id="EssenceGallery-{{ section_id }}"
  data-essence-gallery
  data-interval="{{ gap }}"
>
  <div class="eg-stage">
    <figure class="eg-slide is-on eg-slide--contain">
      {%- comment -%}
        sizes deliberately claims twice the layout width. The frame is 420px,
        so an honest 420 makes the browser fetch a 420 source and render it
        1:1 — which is what made this softer than the gallery it replaced,
        because Dawn was serving a much larger file and letting the browser
        scale it down. Asking for 840 restores that crispness on ordinary
        screens as well as retina ones.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {{
        lead
        | image_url: width: 1946
        | image_tag:
          loading: 'eager',
          sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 840px, 100vw',
          widths: '420, 620, 840, 1100, 1400, 1946',
          alt: lead.alt | default: product.title | escape
      }}
    </figure>
    <figure class="eg-slide eg-slide--cover">
      {%- comment -%}
        The plant photographs are only 600x600, so 600 is everything there is.
        A 420 source was being stretched to fill a 472-tall frame, which is
        where most of the softness came from.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {{
        botanical
        | image_url: width: 600
        | image_tag:
          loading: 'lazy',
          sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 840px, 100vw',
          widths: '420, 600',
          alt: botanical.alt | default: plant_name | escape
      }}
    </figure>
  </div>

  {%- if section.settings.show_plant_caption -%}
    <p class="eg-caption" data-eg-caption>
      <span data-eg-cap-0></span>
      <span data-eg-cap-1 hidden>
        {{- plant_name | escape -}}
        {%- if latin != blank %} &middot; <em>{{ latin | escape }}</em>{% endif -%}
      </span>
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="eg-thumbs">
    <button type="button" class="eg-thumb is-on" data-eg-go="0" aria-label="{{ 'products.product.media.gallery_viewer' | t | default: 'Show the bottle' }}">
      {{ lead | image_url: width: 160 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '80, 160', alt: '' }}
      <span class="eg-bar"></span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="eg-thumb" data-eg-go="1" aria-label="{{ plant_name | escape }}">
      {{ botanical | image_url: width: 160 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '80, 160', alt: '' }}
      <span class="eg-bar"></span>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
